Author: Jagan Mohan R <dr@jm.gl>
Date:   Tue Apr 21 22:16:38 2026 +0530

    h5p(iv): compact WebVTT captions via library CSS (video::cue override)
    
    Append a video::cue rule to the IV library CSS so it loads inside
    the H5P iframe (parent-page ::cue rules can't cross iframe). Brings
    caption text down to 65% of the browser default with a 72%-opaque
    black background and line-height 1.3 — keeps captions from crowding
    the video frame.
    
    Caution (for anyone rebuilding this lib from upstream): the rule
    must be re-appended to dist/h5p-interactive-video.css after each
    webpack build. A future cleaner home would be a separate small
    library (Academe.IVStyles) loaded via library.json preloadedCss.
    
    Follow-up: VTT emitter currently ships one-cue-per-scene so scenes
    with long narrations render as 7-9 line captions. Needs splitting
    into sentence-level cues using scene.narrationWords timings.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

